      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin with, the first step is Course registration."
      ],
      "justification": "Init node captures process commencement; action n2 exactly implements the stated first step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If an exception is needed, then a Request for the exception should be made."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch b1 and guard b1->n4 model the conditional logic; action n4 executes the request; action n3 restates the condition as a check step, which is permitted per modeling rules."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the process can continue."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard v1=false represents the negative exception path where execution proceeds onward as described."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the exception is approved, the next step is course enrollment, followed by seminar group enrollment."
      ],
      "justification": "Three sequential actions faithfully reproduce the approval gate and the two enrollment steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8",
        "action:n9",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the seminar group enrollment is completed, the homework assignment can be started. After working on the homework, it should be turned in. The homework will then be evaluated,"
      ],
      "justification": "Actions precisely follow the sequence of starting, submitting, and evaluating homework."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n12",
        "action:n12",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it was not the last homework, another homework assignment will be given."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch, guard, and actions correctly implement the loop condition and the reassignment step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if it was the last homework, the process can continue."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard v2=true captures the terminal homework condition that allows flow progression."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the same time, two additional steps should be completed: granting accreditation and announcing the date of the exam."
      ],
      "justification": "AND branch models concurrent execution; actions exactly match the two named parallel tasks."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16",
        "action:n17",
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After signing up for the exam, it should be attended. Once the exam is attended, it will be evaluated."
      ],
      "justification": "Sequential actions faithfully restate exam registration, attendance, and evaluation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n20",
        "action:n19",
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the exam is passed, the course is considered passed"
      ],
      "justification": "Branch, guard, and actions accurately implement the pass condition and its outcome."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n21",
        "action:n21"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "if the exam is failed, another sign-up for the exam is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard and action correctly handle the failure retry path."
    }
